From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Don't confuse backing SHM clips with client
 occlusion

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/725

window_surface occlusion clipping describes the GDI backing SHM buffer. It
does not by itself mean that an opaque accelerated client surface covering
the same toplevel must remain below the parent carrier. In particular, a
backing surface may be larger than the actual client area and receive a clip
even though the accelerated client exactly fills the visible window.

The client surface already has its own visual constraint, derived from the
parent's child visibility region. Keep rejecting shaped clients, but do not
reject otherwise eligible own-toplevel clients solely because their backing
SHM surface is clipped. This lets their opaque client surface sit above the
opaque carrier instead of presenting forever underneath a black parent.

The existing alpha, layered, real GDI-over-producer, child, minimized, and
bottom dmabuf guards remain unchanged.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -2434,7 +2434,7 @@ static BOOL wayland_client_surface_should_stack_above_parent(
     if (surface->window.exstyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) return FALSE;
     if (!wayland_surface_is_toplevel(surface) || surface->window.minimized) return FALSE;
     if (!EqualRect(&surface->window.window_rect, &surface->window.client_rect)) return FALSE;
-    if (surface->shaped || surface->occlusion_clipped) return FALSE;
+    if (surface->shaped) return FALSE;
     if (wayland_surface_dmabuf_stack_bottom(surface)) return FALSE;
     return TRUE;
 }
